078 #edb/ref 17592186244359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246582 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "12b31fac-75a2-50ec-9978-bbb512fe8ff1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186245875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246883 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b8644d15-eeb4-52d5-8fd7-da4e9ded447b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247204 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247204 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247204 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247204 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247204 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0172d82e-e716-5982-89be-170e2ffe9720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247204 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,1),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.1+0.25 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "162a4f62-2177-5623-998d-5746dbddde07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247379 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 6-(-7)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{5}{9}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{5}{9}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250989 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250989 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250989 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34813407-d25e-532